{"t": 1795071826.4143438, "kind": "assistant", "text": "The PHP 8.3 upgrade on the dev site caused fatal errors related to the **limit-login-attempts-reloaded** plugin. Since this plugin is active on both dev and production, we must not proceed with the upgrade on production until this is resolved.\n\n### Next Steps:\n1. **Investigate and resolve the plugin incompatibility**:\n   - Check the plugin’s compatibility with PHP 8.3.\n   - Look for an updated version or patch.\n   - If no update is available, consider alternative security measures or temporarily disabling the plugin after taking a snapshot.\n\n2. **Re-test the dev site** after resolving the plugin issue.\n3. **Propose the production change** only after confirming the dev site works correctly with PHP 8.3.\n\nFor now, I will **not** proceed with the production upgrade. Please address the plugin issue and let me know when to re-test dev.\n\n**Action Required**: Fix the `limit-login-attempts-reloaded` plugin for PHP 8.3 compatibility and re-run tests."}
